{{listen|type=music|filename=I Saw Three Ships (Come Sailing In).ogg|title=I Saw Three Ships|description=Performed by Matt Norris & the Moon}}

"'''I Saw Three Ships (Come Sailing In)'''" is an English [[Christmas carol]], listed as [[List of folk songs by Roud number|number 700]] in the [[Roud Folk Song Index]]. The earliest printed version of "I Saw Three Ships" is from the 17th century, possibly [[Derbyshire]], and was also published by [[William Sandys (antiquarian)|William Sandys]] in 1833.<ref>Cecil James Sharp (2008) [https://books.google.com/books?id=3wk3HTOrvmYC&dq=three+ships+-+variant+of+Greensleeves&pg=PA9 The Morris Book: With a Description of Dances as Performed by the Morris Men]</ref><ref name=HYM/> The song was probably traditionally known as "As I Sat On a Sunny Bank",<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ballads Online|url=http://ballads.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/search/advanced/?q_RoudNumbers=700&q_TitleElements=&q_TextBodyElements=&q_Subjects=&q_Themes=&q_ImprintElements=&q_TuneNameElements=&q_Printers=&q_Authors=&q_Notes=&q_References=&searchany=on|access-date=2020-12-15|website=ballads.bodleian.ox.ac.uk}}</ref> and was particularly popular in [[Cornwall]].

== Lyrics and melody==
{{image frame|content=<score sound raw>
\header { tagline = ##f }
\paper { paper-width = 140\mm }
\layout { indent = 0 \context { \Score \remove "Bar_number_engraver" } }

global = { \key as \major \time 6/8 \partial 8 \autoBeamOff }

soprano = \relative c' { \global \set midiInstrument = "flute"
  \repeat volta 2 { es8 | as4 as8 bes4 c8 | es4 c8 bes4 des8 | c4 as8 }
    \alternative { { as4 c8 | bes4 g8 es4 } { as8 bes c bes4. as4 } } \bar "|."
}

alto = \relative c' { \global \set midiInstrument = "flute"
  \repeat volta 2 { es8 | c4 c8 des4 es8 | es4 es8 es4 f8 | es4 es8 }
    \alternative { { es4 es8 es4 es8 es4 } { es8 es es | g4. as4 } }
}

tenor = \relative c { \global \set midiInstrument = "clarinet"
  \repeat volta 2 { es8 | as4 as8 as4 as8 | as4 as8 g4 as8 | as4 c8 }
    \alternative { { c8 (bes) as | g4 bes8 g4 } { c8 bes as | es'4. c4 } }

}

bass = \relative c { \global \set midiInstrument = "bassoon"
  \repeat volta 2 { es8 | as4 as,8 as4 as8 | c4 c8 es4 des8 | as'4 as8 }
    \alternative { { as4 as8 | es4 es8 es4 } { as8 g as | es4. as4 } }
}

verse = \new Lyrics \lyricmode
  { \repeat volta 2 \lyricmode { I saw three ships come sail -- ing in on Christ -- mas }
    \alternative { { day, on Christ -- mas day; } { day in the morn -- ing. } }
}

\score {
  \new ChoirStaff <<
    \new Staff
    <<
      \new Voice = "soprano" { \voiceOne \soprano }
